    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (84.88) and **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29), our clear offensive anchors. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a lucrative combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and a mediocre xERA from Bassitt, while **Gunnar Henderson** faces an ideal matchup against Van Eyk, whose 6.05 xERA provides the highest ceiling of any opposing arm on our slate. The combination of park factors and the aggressive batting order placements for **Drake Baldwin** (72.21) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (69.43) further bolster our top-tier efficiency, with both players capitalizing on strong platoon setups to drive our run production potential.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was undoubtedly **Wade Meckler** (53.83). Despite a high park factor and strong SP skill metrics, he was edged out by the superior power-speed profiles of **Henry Bolte** and **Nasim Nunez**, the latter of whom provides sneaky value due to a slow opposing delivery that increases his stolen base equity\u2014a critical tiebreaker given our emphasis on the scarcity of SBs. Meanwhile, **Kyle Tucker** (75.20) provides the most reliable floor in the outfield today, even against a tougher pitcher in Ray, as his elite consistency keeps him locked into our primary rotation. We are operating without any major weather concerns, though managers should monitor the lineup status for **Nasim Nunez**; should he be moved down further in the order, his efficiency score may require a final internal review before first pitch.",
